**Read:** [Phase Transitions — Bhadeshia and Yan](../sources/Phase-Transitions-Bhadeshia-Yan.lingua#r_2PMPJ2B4GPGDT62S567TX1DCPJ), the complete introduction, thermodynamics, and equilibrium material; [Metals, alloys, steels, and graduate modeling — Bhadeshia teaching materials](../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F), the full introductory metals/alloys and structure/property notes; [General chemistry](../../../../stem/chemistry/general-chemistry/General-chemistry.lingua#r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V), reuse bonding, extended states, phases, and chemical structure as needed.

Electronic states and atomic interactions help explain conductivity, cohesion, and collective response, but an industrial metal is not a defect-free collection of identical atoms. Composition, crystal structure, point/line/interface defects, grains, particles, porosity, and surface history change behavior across scales.

Distinguish a pure element, substitutional/interstitial solution, ordered phase or intermetallic compound, multiphase alloy, and amorphous metallic material. Solubility and phase stability depend on temperature, pressure, composition, and the actual thermodynamic constraints. A phase diagram predicts equilibrium states under a model; an observed material may preserve a processing history that has not equilibrated.

Separate physical properties from structural test response. Resistivity, thermal expansion, elastic stiffness, yielding, work hardening, ductility, fracture, and corrosion involve different mechanisms and conditions. Increasing one desirable property does not automatically improve every other one.

**Work:** choose two documented states of the same alloy or closely related compositions. Connect measured properties with phase/defect/texture evidence and processing history, distinguishing explanation from correlation. Reuse chemical bonding and crystal knowledge where unfamiliar. The later metal-specific studies develop quantitative models and independent experiments rather than treating a familiar alloy label as sufficient understanding.

**Continue:** [Keep composition, structure, process history, and observation scale connected](Composition-structure-processing-and-observation-scales.lingua#r_539959YT1REA5MWMHTT1G8Y2DT).

